1
00:02:31,069 --> 00:02:41,069
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,069 --> 00:02:45,069
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,069 --> 00:02:52,069
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,069 --> 00:02:59,069
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:59,069 --> 00:03:09,069
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,069 --> 00:03:13,069
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:23,069
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:23,069 --> 00:03:33,069
There, they found themselves facing the New Fishman Pirates, who were looking to destroy the Ryugu Kingdom and instigated an all-out war.

9
00:03:33,069 --> 00:03:42,069
After a long and grueling battle, Luffy finally defeated Hordy, the captain of the New Fishman Pirates, thwarting their plan for revenge.

10
00:03:42,069 --> 00:03:52,069
There is still much you do not know. Listen closely. Before you reach the New World, you must be aware of two key changes that have occurred there.

11
00:03:52,069 --> 00:04:01,069
Now then, the first matter, as I've already begun to explain, is that the Navy under Fleet Admiral Sakazuki is stronger than before.

12
00:04:01,069 --> 00:04:11,069
And secondly, the Blackbeard Pirates are making strides of their own.

13
00:04:11,069 --> 00:04:15,069
Ohhhh!

14
00:04:15,069 --> 00:04:20,069
You idiots just had to kick him into next week, didn't you? Why couldn't you just knock him out and tie him up in the tower?

15
00:04:20,069 --> 00:04:23,069
Oh, Nami, you're so cute!

16
00:04:23,069 --> 00:04:26,069
Go catch him and bring him back!

17
00:04:26,069 --> 00:04:33,069
We're here to collect for Big Mom. We can't face them now.

18
00:04:33,069 --> 00:04:39,069
We don't have any sweets for this month's payment. Hordy and his lackeys tore the factory apart.

19
00:04:39,069 --> 00:04:45,069
And all the candy we could salvage was sent to the banquet so the Straw Hats could enjoy it. What should we do?

20
00:04:45,069 --> 00:05:02,069
Something tells me Big Mom of the Four Emperors won't be satisfied with an apology. That woman would level an entire country for sweets.

21
00:05:06,069 --> 00:05:10,069
She loves sweets. Big Mom of the Four Emperors.

22
00:05:10,069 --> 00:05:17,069
After much celebration, the banquet finally comes to an end.

23
00:05:17,069 --> 00:05:20,069
They're seriously gonna let us keep all that treasure?!

24
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:22,069
Cool!

25
00:05:22,069 --> 00:05:24,069
That's pretty generous!

26
00:05:24,069 --> 00:05:28,069
Do you think Luffy and the others are alright, Nami? I'm so worried.

27
00:05:28,069 --> 00:05:30,069
Eh, they're fine.

28
00:05:30,069 --> 00:05:33,069
We're gonna be fancy rich pirates now!

29
00:05:33,069 --> 00:05:37,069
Woo! It sounds nice, but something tells me this is too good to be true.

30
00:05:37,069 --> 00:05:41,069
Hey, Usopp! Why don't we go look for the treasure thief too?

31
00:05:41,069 --> 00:05:47,069
Uh, how about no? I found out that guy's bounty is over 200 million, so he's not gonna be an easy target!

32
00:05:47,069 --> 00:05:50,069
Whoa! And mine's only 50 berries!

33
00:05:50,069 --> 00:05:55,069
Hey, Zoro! Sanji! Check it out! Easiest treasure hunt ever!

34
00:05:55,069 --> 00:05:59,069
That one punch knocked him out cold. I almost feel bad for him.

35
00:05:59,069 --> 00:06:03,069
And he left all this loot sitting out in the open.

36
00:06:03,069 --> 00:06:07,069
Neptune's gonna let us keep all this? I guess he really is as goofy as he looks.

37
00:06:07,069 --> 00:06:10,069
Awesome! How much meat do you think this'll buy?

38
00:06:10,069 --> 00:06:16,069
To think his body could hold all this. I mean, I know he's made a sludge, but still.

39
00:06:16,069 --> 00:06:26,069
One, two, three!

40
00:06:26,069 --> 00:06:28,069
Let's take it back to the palace!

41
00:06:28,069 --> 00:06:29,069
Ow!

42
00:06:29,069 --> 00:06:31,069
We need a flying fish!

43
00:06:31,069 --> 00:06:33,069
Which way to town, Zoro?

44
00:06:33,069 --> 00:06:34,069
That way.

45
00:06:34,069 --> 00:06:36,069
Or we could always run off with the loot.

46
00:06:36,069 --> 00:06:37,069
What?!

47
00:06:37,069 --> 00:06:45,069
Well, Minister of the Left?

48
00:06:45,069 --> 00:06:48,069
Please have mercy, Mr. Pecos.

49
00:06:48,069 --> 00:06:52,069
Hordy and his crew attacked the factory, and now we don't have any candy left.

50
00:06:52,069 --> 00:06:55,069
And what makes any of that our problem?

51
00:06:55,069 --> 00:07:01,069
You're supposed to pay us in candy each month in exchange for using Mama's name.

52
00:07:01,069 --> 00:07:04,069
Don't tell me you've forgotten about our little agreement.

53
00:07:04,069 --> 00:07:07,069
And I was planning on taking some sweets for myself.

54
00:07:07,069 --> 00:07:10,069
