She's probably calling in to check on us.

256
00:16:58,389 --> 00:16:58,689
Really?

257
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:00,849
No, not Big Mom.

258
00:17:00,949 --> 00:17:01,569
She's scary.

259
00:17:21,369 --> 00:17:38,509
You talk to her, Egghead.

260
00:17:38,509 --> 00:17:40,629
She isn't going to like this at all.

261
00:17:42,769 --> 00:17:44,429
Yeah, what's up?

262
00:17:44,429 --> 00:17:51,609
Who is this?

263
00:17:51,949 --> 00:17:53,209
It's Big Mom, right?

264
00:17:53,389 --> 00:17:54,789
What are you doing?

265
00:17:55,049 --> 00:17:55,489
Stop!

266
00:18:02,489 --> 00:18:04,609
You don't sound like Tamago.

267
00:18:04,969 --> 00:18:06,009
Or Pecums.

268
00:18:06,909 --> 00:18:08,109
Who is this?

269
00:18:08,229 --> 00:18:10,049
My name is Monkey D. Luffy.

270
00:18:10,429 --> 00:18:12,129
Soon to be king of the pirates.

271
00:18:12,129 --> 00:18:14,629
Was all that really necessary?

272
00:18:15,149 --> 00:18:16,509
Oh, no moving.

273
00:18:17,209 --> 00:18:18,489
Nice going.

274
00:18:21,269 --> 00:18:23,929
Monkey D.

275
00:18:31,429 --> 00:18:32,149
Ah.

276
00:18:33,509 --> 00:18:35,909
So you must be Garp's grandson.

277
00:18:36,989 --> 00:18:39,229
I remember you, young man.

278
00:18:39,229 --> 00:18:44,849
You're the little upstart who interfered with the war two years ago.

279
00:18:45,009 --> 00:18:46,129
There's no more candy.

280
00:18:46,349 --> 00:18:46,649
Huh?

281
00:18:46,829 --> 00:18:48,209
They can't send you any.

282
00:18:48,629 --> 00:18:50,289
So I heard correctly.

283
00:18:50,669 --> 00:18:52,749
They're supposed to have 10 tons.

284
00:18:53,349 --> 00:18:54,609
Will I eat it all?

285
00:18:54,749 --> 00:18:55,709
It's gone now.

286
00:18:55,769 --> 00:18:56,229
Ah!

287
00:18:59,749 --> 00:19:01,829
You didn't have to tell her that.

288
00:19:01,889 --> 00:19:04,309
What did he just say?

289
00:19:04,309 --> 00:19:05,009
Error!

290
00:19:05,009 --> 00:19:05,409
Oh, sorry!

291
00:19:05,409 --> 00:19:07,009
Oh, no more candy!

292
00:19:07,169 --> 00:19:07,989
Hey!

293
00:19:07,989 --> 00:19:08,269
Oh, my God!

294
00:19:08,269 --> 00:19:09,349
Oh, my God!

295
00:19:09,409 --> 00:19:11,229
Oh, my God!

296
00:19:11,229 --> 00:19:11,269
Jeremy!

297
00:19:11,329 --> 00:19:13,289
Oh, my God!

298
00:19:13,409 --> 00:19:13,569
Oh, my God!

299
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,049
Ah!

300
00:19:14,149 --> 00:19:15,669
Oh, my God!

301
00:19:15,889 --> 00:19:16,169
Oh!

302
00:19:16,349 --> 00:19:17,289
We're here!

303
00:19:17,509 --> 00:19:18,209
Oh!

304
00:19:20,249 --> 00:19:20,269
Ho!

305
00:19:20,449 --> 00:19:21,609
Oh!

306
00:19:23,669 --> 00:19:24,169
Oh!

307
00:19:25,929 --> 00:19:26,709
Oh, my God!

308
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:27,989
Oh, my God!

309
00:19:27,989 --> 00:19:32,189
Oh, my God!

310
00:19:32,189 --> 00:19:33,729
Oh, my God!

311
00:19:33,729 --> 00:19:38,729
Don't you lie to me, you stupid child!

312
00:19:38,729 --> 00:19:42,729
You'd better not be covering for those weak fishmen!

313
00:19:42,729 --> 00:19:45,729
I'm not lying! It was all me!

314
00:19:45,729 --> 00:19:48,729
I didn't know they were supposed to be for you!

315
00:19:52,729 --> 00:19:56,729
I'll make you a deal! We've got a bunch of treasure!

316
00:19:56,729 --> 00:20:00,729
If I give it to you, then can we call it even?

317
00:20:00,729 --> 00:20:02,729
Seriously?!

318
00:20:02,729 --> 00:20:05,729
What?! I can't eat gold and diamonds, can I?

319
00:20:05,729 --> 00:20:09,729
Sweets are the only treasures that mean anything to me!

320
00:20:09,729 --> 00:20:13,729
A minute, monsieur! Are those really full of treasure?

321
00:20:13,729 --> 00:20:15,729
Yeah, they are!

322
00:20:20,729 --> 00:20:23,729
Pardonnez-moi, maman! Let's think about it, no?

323
00:20:23,729 --> 00:20:26,729
So, alors? Only a few short days ago,

324
00:20:26,729 --> 00:20:28,729
that enfant terrible, Captain Kidd,

325
00:20:28,729 --> 00:20:31,729
took down deux of our allies' vessels, n'est-ce pas?

326
00:20:31,729 --> 00:20:33,729
Kid what now?

327
00:20:33,729 --> 00:20:37,729
You know, that rookie we met at Sub Aode, who's worth a hundred million.

328
00:20:40,729 --> 00:20:42,729
It was a disaster!

329
00:20:42,729 --> 00:20:44,729
We suffered a major financial setback,

330
00:20:44,729 --> 00:20:46,729
and we could certainly stun ze monetary assistance!

331
00:20:46,729 --> 00:20:49,729
And no candies are your raison d'être,

332
00:20:49,729 --> 00:20:53,729
but if you ask moi, the best option is to accept ze treasure in lieu of sweets payments for now.

333
00:20:53,729 --> 00:20:57,729
You'll only have to wait a couple of weeks to collect your confections, D'accord?

334
00:20:57,729 --> 00:21:03,729
If you really want something sweet, we can always pick up some bonbons for you on the way back.

335
00:21:04,729 --> 00:21:05,729
Huh?

336
00:21:05,729 --> 00:21:11,729
Do you invite yourself, top uncle?

337
00:21:11,729 --> 00:21:15,729
I don't think you even suggest something like that!

338
00:21:15,729 --> 00:21:19,729
What kind of poor excuse for a pirate compromises on what she wants most?

339
00:21:19,729 --> 00:21:22,729
Oi! Please forgive me, Mama!

340
00:21:22,729 --> 00:21:25,729
Be that as it may...

341
00:21:28,729 --> 00:21:32,729
This insolent pirate who ate all my sweets intrigues me!

342
00:21:32,729 --> 00:21:35,729
Forget Fishmen Island!

343
00:21:35,729 --> 00:21:38,729
Now that you've chosen to go against me,

344
00:21:38,729 --> 00:21:42,729
I'll just have to get my revenge on you instead!

345
00:21:42,729 --> 00:21:54,729
Luffy and the others should be back by now!

346
00:21:55,729 --> 00:21:57,729
I have a bad feeling, Mommy.

347
00:21:57,729 --> 00:21:59,729
What if they're hurt?

348
00:21:59,729 --> 00:22:00,729
You're right.

349
00:22:00,729 --> 00:22:02,729
It is taking them a long time.

350
00:22:02,729 --> 00:22:05,729
What did those goofballs get themselves into now?

351
00:22:05,729 --> 00:22:07,729
If they come back without that treasure,

352
00:22:07,729 --> 00:22:09,729
it will not be pretty!

353
00:22:09,729 --> 00:22:12,729
Well then, Monkey D. Luffy...

354
00:22:13,729 --> 00:22:15,729
Now that I know who you are...

355
00:22:16,729 --> 00:22:17,729
Come here!

356
00:22:17,729 --> 00:22:19,729
Let's chat in the new world!

357
00:22:23,729 --> 00:22:25,729
She means to kill him!

358
00:22:29,729 --> 00:22:31,729
Sure thing! Be there soon!

359
00:22:32,729 --> 00:22:34,729
I've got something I need to settle with you too!

360
00:22:34,729 --> 00:22:35,729
Hmm?

361
00:22:38,729 --> 00:22:39,729
I like this island!

362
00:22:39,729 --> 00:22:41,729
It's too risky to trust you with it!

363
00:22:45,729 --> 00:22:46,729
Once I get there...

364
00:22:47,729 --> 00:22:48,729
I'm gonna kick your ass!

365
00:22:54,729 --> 00:22:57,729
And then I'll make Fishmen Island my territory!

366
00:22:57,729 --> 00:22:58,729
Little brat!

367
00:23:07,729 --> 00:23:09,729
The crisis on Fishmen Island is averted for now,

368
00:23:09,729 --> 00:23:11,729
but a secret hidden inside their royal treasure,

369
00:23:11,729 --> 00:23:12,729
the Tomate Box,

370
00:23:12,729 --> 00:23:16,729
may cause trouble with Big Mom when Luffy reaches the New World.

371
00:23:16,729 --> 00:23:18,729
However, she is but one of many foes

372
00:23:18,729 --> 00:23:20,729
that the Straw Hats have to worry about.

373
00:23:20,729 --> 00:23:22,729
An old adversary has made a move to new waters,

374
00:23:22,729 --> 00:23:24,729
and it's only a matter of time

375
00:23:24,729 --> 00:23:26,729
until they're forced to face off again.

376
00:23:26,729 --> 00:23:27,729
On the next,

377
00:23:27,729 --> 00:23:28,729
One Piece!

378
00:23:28,729 --> 00:23:30,729
Many problems lie ahead!

379
00:23:30,729 --> 00:23:32,729
A trap awaiting in the New World!

380
00:23:32,729 --> 00:23:34,729
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

